    board: file CF-119 + CF-120 — a phantom lock that stalls every lane, and a public main with no protection. Addresses CF-119, CF-120.
    
    Releng tick code-factory-releng-2026-11-03-20-24-59. Both findings were measured on the published tip,
    not recalled: the gate (bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS, rc 0, 10.62 s) and every posture probe
    below were run in a fresh clone of origin/main, because the shared checkout's lane family had four
    sibling ticks running against it while this work was done. The canonical root was never read into the
    work, written to, or cleaned.
    
    CF-119 (P3) — .coding-hermes/board/.lock is a phantom ownership barrier. At the registered workdir
    (HEAD 25d1e71, attached main, parity 0/0, zero tracked edits) the path is a 0-byte file, mtime
    2026-11-03 07:40:02 -05, with no holder (fuser -v and lsof both resolve no process), no consumer
    (git grep -lI 'flock\|fcntl' -- scripts/ prints zero files) and no ignore rule (git check-ignore -q
    exits 1), and it was never committed (git ls-tree HEAD .coding-hermes/board/ lists only tasks.jsonl
    and events.jsonl). 63 board commits landed after its mtime, so it has never excluded a writer. The
    lane's ownership stop treats a board lock as a family-wide barrier, and this lane's own receipts for
    2026-11-02 and for 09:56 / 10:25 / 11:39 today each name it among the blocking artifacts and produced
    no board work. It is also CF-049 AC4's last unsolved condition: every other CF-049 criterion holds as
    of this filing.
    
    CF-120 (P3) — main has no branch protection and no repo ruleset. gh api
    repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/branches/main/protection answers 404 "Branch not protected";
    repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/rulesets answers []. The repository is PUBLIC, so force-push and
    branch deletion are open to every writer. The other half of the required posture passes: secret
    scanning and push protection are enabled (non-provider patterns and validity checks are disabled, as
    are dependabot security updates). Org-level rulesets could not be read with this token (404 plus an
    admin:org scope requirement), so that leg is recorded as unverified rather than absent. Because
    nineteen code-factory lanes and the rest of the fleet land by pushing directly to main and the repo
    ships no GitHub Actions, the row asks for a recorded decision and names the destructive subset
    (force-push, deletion) as the part that is separable from review/status requirements.
    
    Both rows are pending by construction: the repairs are future work tracked by them and are not claimed
    here. Probes were executed from the repo root before filing and re-run after the append; boardctl
    validate -> RESULT: OK (35 warnings, all pre-existing classes plus the probe-outside-canon class this
    board carries on every row); git diff --numstat HEAD^1 HEAD shows 2/0 on tasks.jsonl and 2/0 on
    events.jsonl (insert-only, 92 -> 94 rows, unique ids, 0 duplicates).
    
    Hook note: this is the clone transport and a fresh clone carries no installed commit hook
    (core.hooksPath unset, .git/hooks/pre-commit absent), so no guard hook ran here and none was bypassed;
    the graded gate is the explicit gitreins task complete on this tree.
    
