 {"id":"CF-116","title":"P3 \u2014 the census coverage assertion counts rows, so a mid-run insert mints a duplicate plus a missing row with received == total and the recipe still exits 0","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:20:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:20:00Z","reasoning":["Measured 2026-11-03 by the docs-QA lane at 0c765f6 with the committed stand-in docs/audits/cf116-census-dup-standin.py, which models a project inserted between the two page fetches: page offset=0 serves rows 0..499 of a 600-row list, then the list shifts by one, so page offset=500 serves row 499 a second time and never serves row 500. BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18996 bash docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh prints the count line 600 and 600 row lines and exits 0, while the output holds 599 distinct rows, has no code-factory-p500 line and prints code-factory-p499 twice. CF-089's accepted fix compares received rows against the first reported total (tests/selftest.sh arm 25, fixture mode=short, 'rows received=865 != total reported=866'); that assertion is satisfied exactly by this shape. The row's own trigger class \u2014 a scheduler restart or load-shed between two pages \u2014 also covers an insert between two pages, because offset pagination over a list that mutates mid-run shifts every later offset. Nothing in the tree enumerates identities: the count line comes from wc -l over rows appended blindly with jq -c '.projects[]'. Scheduler project rows carry id=null (GET /api/v1/projects?limit=1), so the identity key is .name."],"acceptance_criteria":["1. Reproduce at the current tree: the probe prints census_rc=0, row_lines=600, distinct_rows=599, p500=MISSING, p499_occurrences=2 \u2014 a complete-looking census that dropped one row and counted another twice. 2. The census asserts identity coverage, not just count: it refuses with a named message and a nonzero exit when an enumerated .name repeats or the distinct count is below the reported total, naming the measured numbers (distinct, duplicates, total) and one concrete duplicated or missing identity. The README.md fence under 'The lanes' and docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh carry the same change and stay textually identical. 3. A tests/selftest.sh arm proves the check can fail: a fixture mode that serves the duplicated boundary row plus the hole prints the named refusal at exit 1 with no census printed, while arms 22-25 still pass unchanged. 4. The live scheduler census still prints 19 rows and exits 0; bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS; scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK."],"probe":"(timeout 40 python3 docs/audits/cf116-census-dup-standin.py --port 18996 >/dev/null 2>&1 &); sleep 2; BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18996 bash docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh >/tmp/cf116-census.out 2>&1; echo \"census_rc=$?\"; echo \"row_lines=$(grep -c '^code-factory-p' /tmp/cf116-census.out)\"; echo \"distinct_rows=$(grep '^code-factory-p' /tmp/cf116-census.out | sort -u | wc -l)\"; if grep -q '^code-factory-p500 ' /tmp/cf116-census.out; then echo \"p500=present\"; else echo \"p500=MISSING\"; fi; echo \"p499_occurrences=$(grep -c '^code-factory-p499 ' /tmp/cf116-census.out)\"","detail":{"filed_by":"code-factory-docs-qa-2026-11-03-19-51-49","reproduced_at":"0c765f6"}}
 {"id":"CF-117","title":"P3 \u2014 the publish-drift census cannot tell a workdir that is merely AHEAD from one that is stale and lossy, so the CF-114 check reds the normal mid-tick state and no gate can run it","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:30:36Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:34:35Z","detail":{"evidence":[]},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 15:2x -05 by the QA lane at origin/main 25d1e71. scripts/board_drift.py:146-147 computes extra = work_rows.keys() - pub_rows.keys() and :155 reports report.row(not extra, 'board extra ids', ...), while :157-162 additionally fails the row-count row on any all_ids non-empty. A canonical checkout that has just appended an uncommitted row \u2014 the state every board commit begins from \u2014 is therefore 'extra': probe output today is `FAIL byte parity tasks.jsonl \u2014 bytes differ`, `FAIL board extra ids \u2014 CF-999`, `FAIL board rows \u2014 91 vs 90 rows; 1 divergent ids: CF-999`, `RESULT: DRIFT (3 failed)`, rc=1. The CF-114 red fixture (one row reopened, one row deleted) prints the SAME verdict word, the same rc, and no direction field, so an operator cannot separate 'one unpushed new row' from 'a stale copy that reverts five closures' (CF-114's P2 defect). Consequences: (a) nothing calls the census except tests/selftest.sh:943 and docs/BOARD.md:47 \u2014 grep for board_drift over *.sh/*.py/*.yaml/*.toml outside those two files returns nothing, so the guard's test_command (bash tests/selftest.sh) and scripts/boardctl validate both green a stale workdir; (b) wiring it in as-is would refuse every board commit, because the commit is always made from an ahead workdir. That makes the CF-114 protection advisory, and a check whose DRIFT verdict is the normal state is decoration by AGENTS.md rule 2.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce on the current tree: the row probe prints `FAIL board extra ids \u2014 CF-999`, a `FAIL  board rows \u2014` line of the form `N+1 vs N rows; 1 divergent ids: CF-999` where N is the published row count at the moment it runs, and `drift_rc=1` \u2014 a workdir that removed and reverted nothing is reported with the same DRIFT verdict as one that lost closures.\n2. The census classifies DIRECTION: a workdir whose id set is a strict superset of the published id set with no status reversal is reported as pending publication (the added ids named in the row, exit 0), while any status reversal or published id missing from the workdir still prints a FAIL naming those ids and exits 1. Both classifications name the measured counts (added, missing, reversed).\n3. tests/selftest.sh arm 29 gains fixture modes proving both directions: an `ahead` fixture (one added row, nothing reverted) exits 0 and names the added id, while the existing `red` fixture (reopened + deleted) still exits 1 and still names both ids; bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.\n4. docs/BOARD.md states the direction semantics and the single command, and scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK at the fixed tip.","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board\" \"$d/p\"; cp .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl \"$d/p/\"; cp \"$d/p/tasks.jsonl\" \"$d/p/events.jsonl\" \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board/\"; printf '%s\\n' '{\"id\":\"CF-999\",\"title\":\"an uncommitted new row\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"P4\",\"complexity\":1,\"reasoning\":\"r\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"a\"}' >> \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl\"; out=$(python3 scripts/board_drift.py check --workdir \"$d/w\" --published-dir \"$d/p\" 2>&1); rc=$?; echo \"$out\" | grep -E 'FAIL|RESULT'; echo \"drift_rc=$rc\""}
 {"id":"CF-118","title":"P4 \u2014 the publish-drift census names no row when the drift is content-only: one row's evidence field reverts, ids and statuses stay identical, and the summary line still PASSes with '0 divergent ids: none'","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:30:36Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:34:35Z","detail":{"evidence":[]},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 15:2x -05 by the QA lane at origin/main 25d1e71. scripts/board_drift.py:141-145 builds `divergent` from STATUS comparison only, and :156-161 derives all_ids from divergent + missing + extra, so a board whose ids and statuses match byte-for-byte per row but whose content differs produces exactly one FAIL \u2014 `byte parity tasks.jsonl \u2014 bytes differ` \u2014 and a PASS row reading `90 vs 90 rows; 0 divergent ids: none`; the number of row ids named anywhere in the FAIL set is 0 (probe prints named_ids=0, drift_rc=1). CF-114 acceptance criterion 4 promised 'a named FAIL naming the divergent row ids'. The realistic shape on this board: closures carry commit_hash plus detail.evidence (CF-114 itself carries 75e94a3b and tree_fp 87ca0eb0...), so a copy taken after a closure but before its evidence backfill reverses only that field while the status reads complete \u2014 the census then reports drift without naming the row an operator must repair, and its own census line says the opposite of what it means. Still fail-closed (exit 1), so this is diagnosability and AC fidelity, not a green-wash.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce on the current tree: the row probe prints `FAIL byte parity tasks.jsonl \u2014 bytes differ`, a `PASS  board rows \u2014` line of the form `N vs N rows; 0 divergent ids: none`, `named_ids=0` and `drift_rc=1` \u2014 the census names no row while asserting that none diverged.\n2. When the bytes differ but the id/status sets agree, the census names the unlike rows by id (a FAIL line carrying the ids whose canonical line differs from the published line), and the board-rows summary no longer reports `0 divergent ids: none` as PASS in that state.\n3. tests/selftest.sh arm 29 gains a content-drift fixture asserting the named id and exit 1, while the existing green fixture still exits 0 and still prints `0 divergent ids: none`; bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.\n4. docs/BOARD.md states that parity is byte-level and that a content-only difference names ids, and scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK at the fixed tip.","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board\" \"$d/p\"; cp .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl \"$d/p/\"; cp \"$d/p/events.jsonl\" \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board/\"; sed 's/\"commit_hash\":\"75e94a3b/\"commit_hash\":\"ffffffff/' \"$d/p/tasks.jsonl\" > \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl\"; out=$(python3 scripts/board_drift.py check --workdir \"$d/w\" --published-dir \"$d/p\" 2>&1); rc=$?; echo \"$out\" | grep -E 'FAIL|board rows|RESULT'; echo \"named_ids=$(echo \"$out\" | grep FAIL | grep -cE 'CF-[0-9]{3}|PERF-[0-9]{3}')\"; echo \"drift_rc=$rc\""}
+{"id":"CF-119","title":"P3 \u2014 .coding-hermes/board/.lock is a phantom ownership barrier: no shipped consumer, no ignore rule, no holder, yet every lane stands down on it","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:40:28Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:40:28Z","detail":{"filed_by":"releng lane","tick":"code-factory-releng-2026-11-03-20-24-59","transport":"fresh clone of origin/main (canonical root untouched: no tracked edits, parity 0/0, attached main)","gate_at_filing":"bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS, rc=0, 10.62 s at 25d1e71"},"reasoning":["Measured 2026-11-03 by releng tick code-factory-releng-2026-11-03-20-24-59 against the registered workdir /home/kara/code-factory at HEAD 25d1e718060f3c9a1ef2c2611e3a0bd3e403a7d1 (attached main, parity 0/0 with origin/main, zero tracked edits): .coding-hermes/board/.lock is a 0-byte file, mtime 2026-11-03 07:40:02 -05. fuser -v reports no holder and lsof resolves no process. git grep -lI 'flock\\|fcntl' -- scripts/ returns ZERO files, so no shipped script opens a lock at that path, and git check-ignore -v says the path is not ignored. git ls-tree HEAD .coding-hermes/board/ lists only tasks.jsonl and events.jsonl, so the file was never committed and is pure working-tree residue.","The file has never excluded a writer: 63 board commits landed after its mtime (git log --since=@$(stat -c %Y .coding-hermes/board/.lock) --oneline -- .coding-hermes/board/ | wc -l prints 63 on 2026-11-03), including the four that closed CF-085/CF-088/CF-114 and filed CF-115/CF-116. A lock that no reader honours is not an ownership barrier; it is an artifact that manufactures one.","Cost, from this lane's own receipts: the code-factory ownership stop classifies 'a board lock' as a family-wide barrier, so every lane whose workdir resolves to this checkout stands down on it. The standing evidence file (~/.hermes/stand-in/releng-lane/code-factory/releng-2026-11-03-evidence.md) records consecutive blocked ticks at 09:56, 10:25, 11:39 on 2026-11-03 and one the day before, each naming .coding-hermes/board/.lock among the blocking artifacts and producing no board work. CF-049 (canonical checkout stuck mid-rebase) AC4 \u2014 'test ! -e ~/code-factory/.coding-hermes/board/.lock' \u2014 cannot pass while the file remains, so this row is also the last obstacle to closing CF-049: every other CF-049 criterion (no rebase marker, attached main, parity 0/0, empty board diff, SELFTEST: PASS at the reconciled head) holds as of this filing.","The adjudication this row asks for is already doctrine but is not shipped as code: the lane must hand-prove consumer, holder and commits-after-mtime every tick, and a hand derivation is re-derived (and can be re-derived wrongly) by every tick that runs it. Nothing in tests/selftest.sh mentions the path, so a regression that starts a real holder cannot be distinguished from residue by the gate."],"acceptance_criteria":["1. .coding-hermes/board/.lock is covered by an ignore rule (git check-ignore -q .coding-hermes/board/.lock exits 0) and the file is gone from the registered workdir after a documented handoff \u2014 OR a shipped consumer/holder exists that makes holding that exact path authoritative, quoted by file and line.","2. A repo-shipped adjudicator (script under scripts/ or a selftest arm) classifies a present lock as HELD only when a live holder is proven (fuser/lsof exit status or an fd probe on /proc/<pid>/fd), and otherwise reports RESIDUE with the consumer-grep count and the commits-after-mtime count.","3. Both arms of that adjudicator are demonstrated on the current tree: a fixture creating an unheld 0-byte lock reports RESIDUE, and a fixture holding the path with flock reports HELD.","4. tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS, with the new arm visible as a named PASS row.","5. The fix does not re-litigate CF-049: closing CF-049 is a separate verification tick that runs its own criteria after this lands."],"probe":"S=$(mktemp -d); printf 'head=%s\\n' \"$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"; printf 'flock_fcntl_consumers_in_scripts='; git grep -lI 'flock\\|fcntl' -- scripts/ | wc -l; printf 'path_ignored='; git check-ignore -q .coding-hermes/board/.lock && echo yes || echo NO; printf 'prose_mentions_outside_docs_and_board='; git grep -lI 'board/\\.lock' -- . ':!docs' ':!*.jsonl' | wc -l; printf 'selftest_arms_naming_it='; grep -c 'board/\\.lock' tests/selftest.sh; if [ -e .coding-hermes/board/.lock ]; then stat -c 'live_lock=%n size=%s mtime=%y' .coding-hermes/board/.lock; else echo 'live_lock=absent-in-this-checkout'; fi; rmdir \"$S\""}
+{"id":"CF-120","title":"P3 \u2014 main has no branch protection and no repo ruleset: force-push and branch deletion are open on the PUBLIC repository every fleet lane pushes to","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:40:28Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:40:28Z","detail":{"filed_by":"releng lane","tick":"code-factory-releng-2026-11-03-20-24-59","secret_scanning":"enabled (with push protection enabled; non-provider patterns and validity checks disabled)"},"reasoning":["Measured 2026-11-03 with gh: repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/branches/main/protection answers HTTP 404 'Branch not protected', and repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/rulesets answers [] \u2014 no repo-level ruleset either. The repository is PUBLIC (gh repo view --json visibility = PUBLIC, isPrivate=false, defaultBranchRef=main, MIT license, pushedAt 2026-11-03T20:20:05Z), so any writer with push access can force-push over main or delete the branch, and the published history is the only copy of this fleet's board and specs.","The public-posture leg this lane is required to check is two-part, and only one part passes: 'secret scanning on' holds (security_and_analysis.secret_scanning.status=enabled and secret_scanning_push_protection.status=enabled), while 'branch protection on' has no counterpart at either the branch or ruleset level. Dependabot security updates are also disabled, and non-provider secret patterns / validity checks are disabled.","Enabling protection is not free here: nineteen code-factory lanes plus the rest of the fleet land by pushing directly to main from agents, and the repo ships no GitHub Actions (gh run list returns [] and .github/workflows is absent), so a profile requiring review approval or required status checks would stop every lane from landing. The destructive subset \u2014 force-push and deletion \u2014 is separable from those requirements, which is why this row asks for a recorded decision rather than assuming protection is desirable.","Scope limit, stated rather than assumed: org-level rulesets could not be read with the available token (GET orgs/coding-hermes/rulesets answers 404 and gh reports it needs admin:org scope), so this row records REPO-level state only. An org ruleset that already blocks force-push would satisfy the intent; that leg is unverified, not absent."],"acceptance_criteria":["1. A recorded decision exists in the repository (docs/ or README \u2014 not a private channel) naming the branch-protection posture for main, and it is one of: (a) a protection profile is enabled, quoting the API response that proves it; or (b) main stays unprotected by decision, naming who decided and what compensating check exists.","2. Under (a): gh api repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/rulesets --jq '[.[].rules[].type]' lists deletion and non_fast_forward (or branches/main/protection reports allow_force_pushes.enabled=false and allow_deletions.enabled=false), and a normal direct lane push still succeeds \u2014 named by its SHA in the evidence.","3. Under (b): the compensating check is re-runnable, e.g. a lane step that compares origin/main to a recorded previous tip and reports a non-fast-forward or deletion.","4. The org-ruleset leg is either resolved with a token that can read org rulesets, or carried explicitly as an open unknown in the decision text.","5. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS at the commit that lands the decision."],"probe":"printf 'branch_protection='; gh api repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/branches/main/protection >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo PRESENT || echo ABSENT; printf 'repo_rulesets='; gh api repos/coding-hermes/code-factory/rulesets --jq 'length'; gh api repos/coding-hermes/code-factory --jq '{visibility, secret_scanning: .security_and_analysis.secret_scanning.status, push_protection: .security_and_analysis.secret_scanning_push_protection.status, dependabot_security_updates: .security_and_analysis.dependabot_security_updates.status}'"}
